# The repository is the archive's skeleton: bin/ (the tools) and 13-ark-node/
# (the node). A clone is meant to become an archive in place: `python bin/ark.py
# fetch` downloads the shelves beside these two folders and `ark.py index` builds
# 10-index/ there. None of that belongs in git.
/0[1-9]-*/
/10-index/
/11-*/
/12-*/
/_incoming/

# Machine-local: the Python environment and llama.cpp (ark.py's defaults are
# <root>/.venv and <root>/llama), this machine's settings, and files the tools
# generate per machine.
/.venv/
/llama/
ark.toml
library.xml
fetch-substitutions.csv
setup-report.txt
MANIFEST.csv
CHECKSUMS.sha256
*.part
*.bad
*.building

__pycache__/
*.pyc
